# .licensing-policy.example  —  template; copy to `.licensing-policy` (drop the .example).
#
# Multi-select policy for how agents apply license headers / attribution when editing ACTUAL CODE.
# See AGENTS-licensing.md for full semantics, the codebase license catalog, and the resolution order.
# Enable a directive by UNCOMMENTING its line. Lines starting with `#` are disabled.
#
# SCOPE: code only (.sv/.svh/.v, .c/.h/.cpp, .py, .S, .tcl, Makefile, .sh, ...).
# NEVER applies to AGENTS*.md, agents/**, specs/**, docs/**, *.md, or LICENSE* files.
# If `.active-contributor` or `.licensing-policy` is missing on an in-scope edit, agents MUST error.

# --- Base directive: what to do when editing an existing code file --------------------------------
# Inherit and PRESERVE the file's own declared SPDX license (never rewrite an existing license).
# DEFAULT_TO_FILE_LICENSE

# --- Selection strategy: how to CHOOSE a license for a NEW file / a file with no header ------------
# Enable AT MOST ONE of the following (two or more => E-MULTISELECT error).
# Most permissive hardware license in the codebase (=> Apache-2.0 WITH SHL-2.1).
# SELECT_MOST_PERMISSIVE
# Most personally-protecting codebase license (patent grant + retaliation + liability limit).
# SELECT_MOST_PROTECTIVE
# Most restrictive codebase license (bounded by the permissive in-repo set; no copyleft present).
# SELECT_MOST_RESTRICTIVE

# --- Personal-contribution directives (apply only to net-new, contributor-authored files) ---------
# Allow the active contributor's new files to carry a different license than the codebase default.
# ALLOW_PERSONAL_LICENSE
# The SPDX id to use when ALLOW_PERSONAL_LICENSE is enabled (required, else E-PERSONAL).
# PERSONAL_LICENSE=LicenseRef-Proprietary
# Write the chosen personal-license notice into new files' headers.
# ADD_PERSONAL_LICENSE_HEADER

# --- Attribution ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Add the active contributor (from .active-contributor) to the file's author/attribution line.
# ADD_CONTRIBUTOR_NAME
